CORE
main.sh

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Subshells (XCU 2.13): ( ), command substitution, pipelines, and
asynchronous lists run with a copy of the shell's state, whose changes
are lost; only the status remains. Assertions inside them are checked.
In dash, $? keeps its value until the command with the command
substitution completes.
